Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Causal Effect Analysis for Species Distribution Models
Version: 0.9.4
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Attributes habitat change to environmental drivers in species
    distribution modelling, and audits when that attribution is identified.
    For each driver, an interventional effect size and a spatially explicit
    effect map are obtained by shifting the driver while holding every other
    driver fixed (g-computation over the fitted ensemble), and a knockout
    necessity diagnostic refits the model without the driver inside every
    spatial fold to measure the held-out discrimination it costs. A driver the
    model responds to but whose removal costs nothing is substitutable by a
    collinear partner, so the pair reports where attribution is not
    identified. Variable selection is a separate, two-stage screen
    (collinearity thinning followed by an importance filter against a
    permutation null) scoped to parsimony and projection robustness. Both sit
    in a complete workflow - Random Forest, BRT, MaxEnt and GAM learners,
    nested spatial cross-validation, ensemble prediction, and future climate
    projection with extrapolation control. The package targets interpretable
    attribution under stated assumptions and does not claim automatic
    discovery of ecological causes.
